# Run with VS Code REST Client or a compatible HTTP client.
# Set accessToken locally to your current Bearer access token (without "Bearer ").
# Never commit a real token or share a copied authenticated request.
# Run requests ONE AT A TIME, in order. Do not use "Run All".
# This creates and edits a disposable note on production; it does not edit your existing note.
# If a request fails, inspect its response before proceeding.
# Deploy the backend with X-Note-Version support BEFORE running this version.
# Do not add If-Match: hosting proxies can apply their own HTTP precondition checks.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@accessToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..gCybfeICGcMEM_a1y4HZVXIFUdCo65rFrSufql6TUUI
@noteId = {{createTestNote.response.body.$.data.id}}

### 1. Create disposable note — expect 201 and data.version = 1.
# @name createTestNote
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Autosave HTTP test — disposable",
  "content": "Before PATCH"
}

### 2. Read current note — expect 200. Record version, ETag, and cache headers.
# Do not rerun this request between steps 3 and 5: step 5 needs its OLD version.
# @name beforePatch
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Cache-Control: no-cache

### 3. PATCH with the version from step 2 — expect 200, NOT 412.
# Expect data.content = "After PATCH" and data.version increased by exactly 1.
# @name firstPatch
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Note-Version: "{{beforePatch.response.body.$.data.version}}"

{
  "content": "After PATCH"
}

### 4. Read after PATCH — expect the content/version returned by step 3.
# If step 3 returned 412 but this GET shows "After PATCH" and an increased version,
# save both responses, timestamps, ETag, and x-vercel-id for investigation.
# @name afterPatch
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Cache-Control: no-cache

### 5. Deliberately replay OLD version — expect 412, with NO database change.
# Only run after verifying step 3 SUCCEEDED and step 4 shows the new version.
# @name stalePatch
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Note-Version: "{{beforePatch.response.body.$.data.version}}"

{
  "content": "THIS MUST NOT BE SAVED"
}

### 6. Verify rejection did not change anything — expect same data as step 4.
# @name afterRejection
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Cache-Control: no-cache

### 7. Optional cleanup: move ONLY the disposable note to Trash — expect 200.
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteId}}/trash
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Note-Version: "{{afterRejection.response.body.$.data.version}}"
